  "lesson": {
    "instructions": "Use i (index) on G, m (middle) on B and a (ring) on high E. Count 1, 2-and, 3-and: hold the first pluck for one beat, then play four eighth notes. Use p (thumb) for the written bass. Pluck bass and G together on beat 1, then B, high E, B, G. Keep the same right-hand pattern. Play C-C-G-G-D-D-G-G, one pattern per bar. Rest for one bar, then repeat the whole eight-bar piece. Hold each shape while picking only the written strings. This is an original chord study, not a separate sung melody.",
